    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The chief seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> family on the Trucial Coast from the early nineteenth century.</li><li>It lived from pearling, fishing and trade, under British protection after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-maritime-treaty-of-1820">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</a>.</li><li>Losing dependencies and trade to its neighbours, it joined the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> as a founding member in 1971.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Sharjah had the first airfield on the Trucial Coast: in 1932 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-airways">Imperial Airways</a> built a fortified rest house there, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mahatta-fort">Al Mahatta</a>, for passengers flying between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

